ADR-0004 point 2 table (2026-10-15): HEAD holds only a gitlink for a
submodule, so its contents are not committed and a fresh clone never
has them. A populated submodule is now skipped by default, disclosed
("Installed dependency source not analysed: lib/sub/ (git submodule).
..."), and analysed as tier 3 with --trace-deps <declared path>.

Detection by evidence, not name: discovery.SUBMODULE_RULE claims a
directory that holds a .git (one lstat is all an ordinary directory
pays), that the enclosing work tree's .gitmodules declares, and whose
HEAD entry is a gitlink (mode 160000), read with git ls-tree HEAD like
_head_entries (never the index); with no git or no commits, a .git
file. The git call is factored into _ls_tree_head so the hazard
handling lives once. An unpopulated submodule (empty directory) and an
undeclared nested repository are unchanged.

Tests build a real superproject with `git submodule add`: skipped and
disclosed, traced as tier 3 with package lib/sub, a plain clone's
empty submodule is a no-op.

